    <section id="about">
      <div class="section-head reveal">
        <h2 class="section-title">About</h2>
        <span class="section-index">01 / 04</span>
      </div>
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div class="reveal">
          <p>I'm an <b>Electrical Engineering undergraduate</b> who likes working close to the hardware — where a signal from a sensor becomes a decision an Arduino can act on. My interest sits at the intersection of <b>circuits, embedded code, and real-world safety problems</b>.</p>
          <p>Alongside coursework, I compete at the <b>BME Hackathon</b> and the <b>PPS Hackathon (Programme for Problem Solving)</b>, applying electrical engineering fundamentals and structured programming logic to real challenges under time pressure — sharpening how fast I can move from idea to working prototype.</p>
          <p>Right now my focus is my minor project: an <b>Alcohol Detection &amp; Alert System</b>, built to show how a simple sensor circuit can trigger a meaningful safety response.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="spec-card reveal">
          <div class="row"><span>role</span><span>EE Undergraduate</span></div>
          <div class="row"><span>focus</span><span>Embedded Systems</span></div>
          <div class="row"><span>hardware</span><span>Arduino</span></div>
          <div class="row"><span>languages</span><span>Python, C, C++</span></div>
          <div class="row"><span>competitions</span><span>BME · PPS Hackathon</span></div>
          <div class="row"><span>status</span><span class="live">Building</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

